Note added on 06 JAN 2025:

The Ramses code was moved from Bitbucket to GitHub.
In response, I move this clone following the steps listed in:

https://ramses.cnrs.fr/ramses-moves-to-github/

Note that there were some conflicts to be resoloved affecting:

README.md
rt/rt_init_flow_fine.f90

These were resolved with the following steps:

$> git mergetool

opens FileMerge and allows to make the required edits, and save the
file with the appropriate name (i.e. overwrite the relevant [not the open] file)
and quit. Each file needing merging will open in turn.

I then needed to commit the changes via:

$> git commit -m "Resolved conflicts in Bitbucket-GitHub migration"

and finally,

$> git pull --no-rebase

Then, check that everything is as it should via:

$> git remote update ;  git status

The local repo will be ahead with respect to the remote by a number of commits,
so I need to push these. To allow for a passwordless process, first I needed
to change the repo's URL via (did not need to do this for Bitbucket...):

$> git remote set-url origin git+ssh://git@github.com/ttepperg/ramses.git

Then

$> git push




